# Packet Tracer Lab: Configure CDP, LLDP, and NTP

## Overview

This repository documents my completion of the Cisco Packet Tracer activity **"Configure CDP, LLDP, and NTP."** The lab involved discovering an undocumented network topology, configuring discovery protocols (CDP and LLDP) with directional control, and setting up NTP synchronization on a router.

**Final Score: 100%** ✅

---

## Lab Objectives

- Configure CDP to run globally on a device
- Disable CDP on device interfaces where necessary
- Configure LLDP to run globally on a device
- Configure LLDP to send and receive messages according to requirements
- Configure a router to use an NTP server

