## What I Completed

### 1. LLDP Configuration (HQ Router + HQ Switches)

**HQ Router:**
- Disabled CDP globally (`no cdp run`)
- Enabled LLDP globally (`lldp run`)
- Configured G0/0/0 and G0/0/1 to **receive-only** LLDP (`no lldp transmit` + `lldp receive`)

**HQ-SW-1 and HQ-SW-2:**
- Disabled CDP globally
- Enabled LLDP globally
- Configured uplinks to **send-only** LLDP (`no lldp receive` + `lldp transmit`)
- Disabled LLDP completely on in-use access ports (`no lldp transmit` + `no lldp receive`)

**Verification:** `show lldp neighbors` on HQ confirmed both switches were discovered, proving the one-way LLDP path worked.

### 2. CDP Configuration (Branch Router + Branch Switches)

- Enabled CDP globally on the Branch router (`cdp run`)
- Discovered the three Branch switch management IPs via `show cdp neighbors detail`
- SSH'd into each Branch switch (no CLI access by clicking)
- Disabled CDP on in-use access ports only (`no cdp enable` on Fa0/1 for BR-SW-2 and BR-SW-3)
- BR-SW-1 had no access ports in use (all connected ports were trunks) — no configuration needed

### 3. NTP Configuration (HQ Router)

```cisco
ntp server 192.168.1.254
```

**Verification:**
```
Clock is synchronized, stratum 2, reference is 192.168.1.254
```

